<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="60567" href="schedule/2016/spring/MACS/383/60567.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2016" href="schedule/2016.xml">2016</calendarYear><term id="120161" href="schedule/2016/spring.xml">Spring 2016</term><subject id="MACS" href="schedule/2016/spring/MACS.xml">Media and Cinema Studies</subject><course id="383" href="schedule/2016/spring/MACS/383.xml">French &amp; Comparative Cinema II</course></parents><sectionNumber>NB </sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>FR 389, Spring 2016 An introductory survey of contemporary French women directors. Particular focus on the gendered gaze, spectatorship, and film form. While discussing the themes and topics of select mainstream and experimental films, we will theorize the development of a feminine aesthetic in editing, camera work, and narrative art. Readings by Mulvey, Flitterman-Lewis, De Lauretis, Tarr &amp; Rollet, and others. Films by G. Dulac, A. Varda, D. Kurys, C. Denis, C. Akerman, M. Duras, C. Serreau, C. Breillat, D. Gleize, A. Jaoui. Taught in English.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2016-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2016-05-04Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>223</roomNumber><buildingName>David Kinley Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Poucel" firstName="J">Poucel, J</instructor></instructors></meeting><meeting id="1"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>06:30 PM</start><end>08:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>148</roomNumber><buildingName>Armory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Poucel" firstName="J">Poucel, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meeting